From c21623911347ed9bcb8802fef89cddb62ec7fe64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:40:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(rust-rounds): take the deletion hold before reading held
 weeks (RR25)

`queue_held_weeks` read every held week of Rust Rounds before it took the
deletion hold, on a connection it then kept while it waited for the hold,
and queued what it had read. A deletion that landed in between left the
sweep queueing weeks read from an account already gone.

- The sweep now does as `keep` does: the deletion hold first, then one
  `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` transaction, and the held weeks are read inside it,
  so it queues only what the subject holds once no deletion is in flight.
  It no longer holds a connection while it waits for the hold.
- With no week that reads, the transaction commits having written nothing
  where the sweep used to return before taking the hold; what it queues,
  logs and returns is unchanged.
- Tests beside the pass tests: the sweep runs once per process and again
  after a restart; a failed sweep (an insert the test makes fail) is
  reported and tried again at the next pass; a held file that does not
  read as its week is passed over while the week beside it is queued; and
  a deletion that lands while the sweep waits leaves nothing queued, which
  the old order failed (it held the test pool's one connection and the
  deletion never ran). The upgrade test's own copy of the hold setup is
  now the shared `hold_unqueued`.

Change-Kind: story
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
